<p>NOTES:  (A) In accordance with the Financial Accounting Standards Board Statement No. 121, &quot;Accounting for the Impairment of Long-Lived Assets and for Long-Lived Assets to Be Disposed Of,&quot; in June 1996, the Company recorded a loss to write off certain intangible assets in the Healthcare division of its General Information Services segment.</p>
<p>(B) In November, 1995, the Company and the California State Lottery (CSL) finalized the terms of a reinstated contract.  The unusual item above reflects an initial settlement of $25 million received from the CSL less related costs.</p>
<p>(C) During the fourth quarter, 1995, the Company incurred restructuring charges related to the discontinuance of certain product lines and the streamlining of operations in its business segments.</p>
<p>(D) During the fourth quarter, 1996, the Company sold all of the business units in its Health Information Services group. These sales resulted in an $11.6 million gain reported in Other income, net ($1.6 million after tax, or $.01 per share). SOURCE Equifax Inc.</p>
